/*
  PLACEHOLDER FILE — REPLACE BEFORE DEPLOYING TO USERS WHO NEED .xlsx / .xls SUPPORT
  ====================================================================================

  This build environment has no internet access, so the real third-party
  SheetJS "xlsx.min.js" library (used to parse .xlsx and .xls files in the
  browser) could not be downloaded and bundled automatically.

  The dashboard is fully functional without this file for CSV files, because
  Dashboard/js/dashboard.js includes its own built-in CSV parser. Only .xlsx
  and .xls uploads require this library — the dashboard detects its absence
  and shows a clear on-screen message instead of crashing.

  TO ENABLE .xlsx / .xls SUPPORT (one-time, offline-friendly, no build step):
  1. On any computer with internet access, download the community SheetJS
     library file named "xlsx.min.js" (or "xlsx.full.min.js") from the
     official SheetJS distribution (e.g. the version published on npm as the
     "xlsx" package, dist/xlsx.full.min.js).
  2. Rename it to "xlsx.min.js" if needed.
  3. Replace this placeholder file at Dashboard/js/xlsx.min.js with the
     downloaded file.
  4. No other change is required — Dashboard.html already references
     "js/xlsx.min.js" via a local <script> tag, and dashboard.js will detect
     the library automatically the next time Dashboard.bat is launched.

  Until step 3 is done, .xlsx/.xls uploads will show:
  "The xlsx.min.js library was not found in the js/ folder..."
*/
